  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Monochromatic light of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>14</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> is produced by a laser. The power emitted is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>.</mo></math> How many photons per second on an average, are emitted by the source?</p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>)</p>"
  },
